# LF line endings in every checkout, Windows included: Git for Windows otherwise
# turns text files into CRLF on checkout, which breaks the bash scripts
# (install.sh, bin/cubex) and makes whole-file phantom diffs. Binary files
# (images, GIFs) are detected and left alone.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Keep the README screenshots and demo GIFs out of GitHub's source tarballs,
# which is what install.sh and `cubex update` download.
docs/media export-ignore
